## ENGLISH

This unified academic package is distributed under a three-component scheme:
**code** under MIT (see `LICENSE-CODE`), **text** under CC BY 4.0 (see
`LICENSE-TEXT`), and **data** under ODbL 1.0 (see `LICENSE-DATA`). This
umbrella file states the research-integrity conditions that apply on top of
the three component licences.

### 1. Ownership

All copyright, related and neighbouring rights to the research content of
this package — the monographs, the verification suites, the figures, the data
compilations, the presentations and the documentation — belong **fully and
exclusively** to **Isaev Iskhak Khamzatovich** (the "Author"). No joint ownership, licence
back, or implied transfer arises from publication of this package.

### 2. Permissions granted

Without a separate written agreement you may:

1. **View and read** any part of this package;
2. **Clone and fork** for private, non-commercial academic study;
3. **Run** the code locally for scholarly verification and reproducibility
   checks;
4. **Cite** the work and quote short excerpts (with full attribution to the
   Author, the DOI [10.5281/zenodo.21825394](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21825394) and a link to this package);
5. **Redistribute** code under the terms of MIT, text under CC BY 4.0 and
   data under ODbL, subject to the component licences.

### 3. The honesty clause (inviolable)

The honesty layer of this package — the `does_not_prove` fields, the blocked
verdicts of the V13 obligation machine, the negative-results register — is
**part of the scientific record**. Any derivative work that presents the
numerical results of this programme without the corresponding honest boundary
statements misrepresents the science and violates the licence. When in doubt:
quote the boundary verbatim.

### 4. Restrictions

You may NOT, without separate written permission from the Author:

1. Present the numerical or formal results of this programme as a proof of the
   Riemann hypothesis (the package itself blocks this conclusion);
2. Commercialize the monographs or their translations;
3. Remove or alter attribution, the honesty clause, or the provenance records.

### 5. Everything else

Requests: through the repository issue tracker. The Author grants no warrant-
ies; the package is provided "as is", for scholarly study.

